{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdlib>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long best_num = 100000, best_den = 1;\nlong long best_a = 0, best_b = 0;\n\nlong long my_gcd(long long x, long long y) {\n    x = x < 0 ? -x : x;\n    y = y < 0 ? -y : y;\n    if (x == 0) return y;\n    if (y == 0) return x;\n    return y ? my_gcd(y, x % y) : x;\n}\n\nvoid try_candidate(long long x, long long y, long long b, long long a) {\n    if (a < 0) return;\n    \n    long long g = my_gcd(a, b);\n    a /= g;\n    b /= g;\n    \n    long long num = llabs(b * x - a * y);\n    long long den = b * y;\n    g = my_gcd(num, den);\n    num /= g;\n    den /= g;\n    \n    if (num * best_den < best_num * den) {\n        best_num = num;\n        best_den = den;\n        best_a = a;\n        best_b = b;\n    } else if (num * best_den == best_num * den) {\n        if (b < best_b || (b == best_b && a < best_a)) {\n            best_a = a;\n            best_b = b;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    for (long long i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        try_candidate(x, y, i, (i * x) / y);\n        try_candidate(x, y, i, (i * x) / y + 1);\n        try_candidate(x, y, i, (i * x) / y - 1);\n    }\n    \n    cout << best_a << \"/\" << best_b << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static long best_num = 100000;\n    static long best_den = 1;\n    static long best_a = 0;\n    static long best_b = 0;\n\n    static long my_gcd(long x, long y) {\n        x = x < 0 ? -x : x;\n        y = y < 0 ? -y : y;\n        if (x == 0) return y;\n        if (y == 0) return x;\n        return y != 0 ? my_gcd(y, x % y) : x;\n    }\n\n    static void try_candidate(long x, long y, long b, long a) {\n        if (a < 0) return;\n        \n        long g = my_gcd(a, b);\n        a /= g;\n        b /= g;\n        \n        long num = Math.abs(b * x - a * y);\n        long den = b * y;\n        g = my_gcd(num, den);\n        num /= g;\n        den /= g;\n        \n        if (num * best_den < best_num * den) {\n            best_num = num;\n            best_den = den;\n            best_a = a;\n            best_b = b;\n        } else if (num * best_den == best_num * den) {\n            if (b < best_b || (b == best_b && a < best_a)) {\n                best_a = a;\n                best_b = b;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long x = scanner.nextLong();\n        long y = scanner.nextLong();\n        long n = scanner.nextLong();\n        \n        for (long i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n            try_candidate(x, y, i, (i * x) / y);\n            try_candidate(x, y, i, (i * x) / y + 1);\n            try_candidate(x, y, i, (i * x) / y - 1);\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(best_a + \"/\" + best_b);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>"